cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Uncertainty-aware gaze-to-cell mapping for mobile eye tracking of visual search on a physical board"
abstract: >-
  Processing pipeline that converts Pupil Labs Core recordings of a physical
  visual search task (an 8x5 board of coloured pieces searched and touched by
  the participant) into per-trial, per-cell gaze data without manual coding of
  the trials. It combines ArUco-based board localization with a deterministic
  cell grid, automatic trial segmentation from the sample panels, a gated
  post-hoc drift correction from the calibration panels recovered in the scene
  video, and a per-participant gaze uncertainty model propagated to a
  probability mass per board cell and a graded target-found confidence.
